Clinical Interventions: IMMEDIATELY activated emergency medical services (000 - Priority 1). Administered Intramuscular Morphine 10mg STAT for sympathetic pain control (to assist in lowering shear forces on the aorta). Instructed patient to remain strictly supine and absolutely still to minimize blood pressure spikes.
Positive Behavioral Change:
Action: Remain perfectly still on the sofa, breathing slowly and deeply. Consequence: Minimization of heart rate and blood pressure spikes, reducing the sheer stress on the tearing blood vessel and slightly dulling the agonizing pain (negative reinforcement).
Action: N/A - Behavioral interventions are secondary to immediate survival and surgical transport.
